{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.rank_eq_magic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.rank_eq_magic","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/MagicNumbersBring.lean#L55-L55","doc":"**Conjectural rank identity.**  For every magic number `n`, the\nattached distinguished lattice has `ℤ`-rank exactly `n` — the\nrank-preserving bijection `𝔐 ↔ {Lₙ}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.magicLattice","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.magicLattice","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/MagicNumbersBring.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The distinguished `S₅`-stable, `τ̂`-stable period sub-lattice\nattached to a magic number, presented by its `ℤ`-rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/MagicNumbersBring.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.MagicNumbersBring","kind":"class","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/MagicNumbersBring.lean#L37-L55","doc":"**Conjecture class** (`conj:magic-numbers-bring`).\n\nAn instance asserts a rank-`n` integer lattice `magicLattice n` (a\ndistinguished `S₅`-stable, `τ̂`-stable period sub-lattice of a power of\n`H₁(𝓑, ℤ)`) for every magic number `n ∈ magicNumbers`, whose `ℤ`-rank\n**equals** `n`.\n\nThe field `rank_eq_magic` carries the conjecture's genuine content — the\nrank-preserving bijection between magic numbers and the distinguished\nlattices — rather than a bare `True`.  This is a **primary** conjecture\n(its signature takes no other conjecture class as a hypothesis). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:magic-numbers-bring","label":"conj:magic-numbers-bring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/magic-numbers-bring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Conjectures.magicNumbers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Conjectures.magicNumbers","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Conjectures/MagicNumbersBring.lean#L34-L35","doc":"The seven observed nuclear magic numbers `{2, 8, 20, 28, 50, 82, 126}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}